<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  a4kStreaming home (tvOS-like). Coordinates are 1080p pixels = dobby units x2. No includes and no named colours: a
  script window resolves both against the active skin (report 010-phase2, spike 7). Fonts are Estuary's names; an
  unknown name falls back to font13.

  Rows are the plugin's own listings, loaded by Kodi on job threads. Their URL is a window property set before the
  window opens; an empty property loads nothing and hides the row. A row is visible while it loads or has items: a
  hidden container never takes the items its provider fetched (spike 2b). Each row has a no-op onclick so Kodi does not
  play or open the item itself; Python handles the click in onAction (spike 2c).

  The page grouplist links only its direct children, the groups; the lists and buttons inside them get no up/down
  from it. So each focusable control names its neighbour groups in onup/ondown, and a hidden group passes the move on
  through the links the grouplist gave it. A container or grouplist with no onleft/onright/ondown wraps around at its
  edge, so the edges say noop.
-->
